Action execution constraints plus shared-cache correctness hold.

Dx pipeline plus evaluator actions carry no-remote-exec (never remotely
executed, still locally cacheable); the shared BuildBuddy remote cache
passes the `.bazelrc` `ci` config plus the BuildBuddy API-key header
inline on every Bazel plus dx call (`$BAZEL_CONFIG $BB_ARGS`), PR runs
upload nothing via `ci-pr` (issue #1059), an absent key sets no
remote-cache flag (local-cache only), the secretless dry run
stays local, and the legacy actions/cache disk cache stays deleted (no
restore-keys, no hashFiles keys, no per-host prefixes); aquery
ExecutionInfo plus ActionKey shape plus the local execution-log
hit/miss half prove invalidation locally while remote execution stays
unverified.
